        <headline>special weather statement in effect</headline>
        <description>
What:
Moderate to strong gusty winds.

When:
Now till this evening.

Where:
- Lakes District
- Chilcotin
- Cariboo
- Fraser Canyon
- 100 Mile House
 - Highway 97 - Clinton to 100 Mile House via Begbie Summit
- South Thompson
- Nicola
- Coquihalla Highway
- Okanagan Connector

Additional information:
Another strong low pressure system is approaching the B.C. coast, bringing a prolonged period of southeasterly winds with gusts ranging from 60 to 80 km/h across the B.C. Interior. These winds are expected to peak this morning. Winds will then ease slightly before an incoming cold front brings a strong push of southwesterly winds, with gusts potentially reaching 90 km/h starting late this morning for western regions. These gusty winds are expected to ease by this evening.

Local utility outages are possible. 
Secure loose objects.
High-sided vehicles will be pushed around by the wind.
Parks and forests will likely sustain some damage.

###

Weather in the mountains can change suddenly resulting in hazardous driving conditions.

Road conditions are available at https://www.drivebc.ca/.

Please continue to monitor alerts and forecasts issued by Environment Canada. To report severe weather, send an email to BCstorm@ec.gc.ca or post reports on social media using #BCStorm.
</description>
